      "ply": 65,
      "t": 659.5,
      "fen": "8/p1p2pK1/8/8/3pkP2/6P1/PP6/8 b - - 1 33",
      "line": [
        "Kg7"
      ],
      "spoken": "White shuffles the king to g7's approach.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 66,
      "t": 661.5,
      "fen": "8/p1p3K1/8/5p2/3pkP2/6P1/PP6/8 w - - 0 34",
      "line": [
        "f5"
      ],
      "spoken": "We push f5 — not even giving up a single pawn.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 68,
      "t": 673,
      "fen": "8/p1p5/6K1/5p2/4kP2/3p2P1/PP6/8 w - - 0 35",
      "line": [
        "Kg6",
        "d3"
      ],
      "spoken": "If White plays g4 we take it; both pawns are unstoppable. f5 is clinical, and we push d3.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 70,
      "t": 675.5,
      "fen": "8/p1p5/6K1/8/4kPp1/3p4/PP6/8 w - - 0 36",
      "line": [
        "g4",
        "fxg4"
      ],
      "spoken": "After g4 we can capture, and after f5 either passer runs.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 71,
      "t": 679,
      "fen": "8/p1p5/6K1/5P2/4k1p1/3p4/PP6/8 b - - 0 36",
      "line": [
        "f5"
      ],
      "spoken": "We can even push the g-pawn to promote with check.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 72,
      "t": 684.5,
      "fen": "8/p1p5/6K1/5P2/4k1p1/8/PP1p4/8 w - - 0 37",
      "line": [
        "d2"
      ],
      "spoken": "The simpler route is d2 and d1, promoting to a queen.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 76,
      "t": 700,
      "fen": "8/p1p2P2/3r2K1/8/4k1p1/8/PP6/8 w - - 1 39",
      "line": [
        "f6",
        "d1=R",
        "f7",
        "Rd6+"
      ],
      "spoken": "There's a laborious way and an easy way — the easy way gives the queen for the pawn, then promotes the other one.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 77,
      "t": 703.5,
      "fen": "8/p1p2PK1/3r4/8/4k1p1/8/PP6/8 b - - 2 39",
      "line": [
        "Kg7"
      ],
      "spoken": "If you want to be clinical, you don't even give up the queen — you use it to shepherd White's king off the pawn, since there are no stalemate worries here.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 10,
      "t": 739.5,
      "fen": "r1bqk2r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/2b5/3NP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 1 6",
      "line": [],
      "spoken": "A solid, simple positional game, and we're winning more of these as we climb — the bishop to c5 is a good line for an e5 player.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 11,
      "t": 746,
      "fen": "r1bqk2r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/2b5/3NP3/2N1B3/PPP2PPP/R2QKB1R b KQkq - 2 6",
      "line": [
        "Be3"
      ],
      "spoken": "After the bishop to c5, White has the knight to c6, but the bishop to e3 is another popular try.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 10,
      "t": 759,
      "fen": "r1bqk2r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/2b5/3NP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 1 6",
      "line": [],
      "spoken": "There's also the knight to f5 here — a theoretical line worth your own research.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 12,
      "t": 764,
      "fen": "r1bqk2r/p1pp1ppp/2p2n2/2b5/4P3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 0 7",
      "line": [
        "Nxc6",
        "bxc6"
      ],
      "spoken": "After the trade on c6 and the bishop to g5...",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 13,
      "t": 765.5,
      "fen": "r1bqk2r/p1pp1ppp/2p2n2/2b3B1/4P3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R2QKB1R b KQkq - 1 7",
      "line": [
        "Bg5"
      ],
      "spoken": "...that's again one of several possible moves.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 12,
      "t": 768.5,
      "fen": "r1bqk2r/p1pp1ppp/2p2n2/2b5/4P3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 0 7",
      "line": [],
      "spoken": "Just one variation among many.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 13,
      "t": 771,
      "fen": "r1bqk2r/p1pp1ppp/2p2n2/2b5/4P3/2NB4/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R b KQkq - 1 7",
      "line": [
        "Bd3"
      ],
      "spoken": "The bishop to d3 is actually the main line, the most popular move.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 14,
      "t": 776,
      "fen": "r1bqk2r/p1p2ppp/2pp1n2/2b5/4P3/2NB4/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 0 8",
      "line": [
        "d6"
      ],
      "spoken": "Then the line runs d6 — and that's the key difference between the bishop on c5 versus b4.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 9,
      "t": 784,
      "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/8/3NP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 0 5",
      "line": [],
      "spoken": "With the bishop developed to b4, d6 is a move, but...",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 13,
      "t": 787.5,
      "fen": "r1bqk2r/p1pp1ppp/2p2n2/8/1b2P3/2NB4/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R b KQkq - 1 7",
      "line": [
        "Bb4",
        "Nxc6",
        "bxc6",
        "Bd3"
      ],
      "spoken": "...after the bishop to d3, almost everyone plays d5 instead.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 14,
      "t": 788.5,
      "fen": "r1bqk2r/p1p2ppp/2p2n2/3p4/1b2P3/2NB4/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 0 8",
      "line": [
        "d5"
      ],
      "spoken": "That d5 is the standard follow-up with the bishop on b4.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 13,
      "t": 793.5,
      "fen": "r1bqk2r/p1pp1ppp/2p2n2/8/1b2P3/2NB4/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R b KQkq - 1 7",
      "line": [],
      "spoken": "With the bishop developed to c5, on the other hand, you are going for d6.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 15,
      "t": 795,
      "fen": "r1bqk2r/p1pp1ppp/2p2n2/2b5/4P3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 3 8",
      "line": [
        "Bc5",
        "Bf1"
      ],
      "spoken": "Either way, the bishop to g5 is still a move.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 13,
      "t": 796.5,
      "fen": "r1bqk2r/p1pp1ppp/2p2n2/8/1b2P3/2NB4/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R b KQkq - 1 7",
      "line": [],
      "spoken": "In any case, the bishop to g5 is playable.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 17,
      "t": 798.5,
      "fen": "r1bq1rk1/p1pp1ppp/2p2n2/2b3B1/4P3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R2QKB1R b KQ - 5 9",
      "line": [
        "Bc5",
        "Bf1",
        "O-O",
        "Bg5"
      ],
      "spoken": "So we castle, White plays the bishop to e2, and we throw in h6.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 15,
      "t": 799.5,
      "fen": "r1bqk2r/p1pp1ppp/2p2n2/2b5/4P3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 3 8",
      "line": [],
      "spoken": "Filing this line away.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 19,
      "t": 801,
      "fen": "r1bq1rk1/p1pp1pp1/2p2n1p/2b3B1/4P3/2N5/PPP1BPPP/R2QK2R b KQ - 3 10",
      "line": [
        "h6",
        "Bg5",
        "O-O",
        "Be2"
      ],
      "spoken": "I think the bishop to e2 was already inaccurate.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 17,
      "t": 802.5,
      "fen": "r1bqk2r/p1pp1pp1/2p2n1p/2b3B1/4P3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R2QKB1R b KQkq - 1 9",
      "line": [],
      "spoken": "White didn't realise the e4-pawn is a serious weakness here.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 21,
      "t": 818,
      "fen": "r1bq1rk1/p1p2pp1/2pp1n1p/2b5/4P2B/2N5/PPP1BPPP/R2QK2R b KQ - 3 11",
      "line": [
        "d6",
        "Bh4",
        "O-O",
        "Be2"
      ],
      "spoken": "Had White known, the bishop to d3 supports the pawn. So we play h6, the rook to e8, and d6.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 23,
      "t": 819.5,
      "fen": "r1bqr1k1/p1p2pp1/2pp1n1p/2b5/4P2B/2N5/PPP1BPPP/R2Q1RK1 b - - 5 12",
      "line": [
        "Re8",
        "O-O"
      ],
      "spoken": "We make all the typical moves.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 21,
      "t": 821.5,
      "fen": "r1bq1rk1/p1p2pp1/2pp1n1p/2b5/4P2B/2N5/PPP1BPPP/R2QK2R b KQ - 3 11",
      "line": [],
      "spoken": "And the bishop to f3...",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 23,
      "t": 822.5,
      "fen": "r1bqr1k1/p1p2pp1/2pp1n1p/2b5/4P2B/2N5/PPP1BPPP/R2Q1RK1 b - - 5 12",
      "line": [
        "Re8",
        "O-O"
      ],
      "spoken": "...is probably a mistake, assuming our whole idea is sound.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 21,
      "t": 824,
      "fen": "r1bq1rk1/p1p2pp1/2pp1n1p/2b5/4P2B/2N5/PPP1BPPP/R2QK2R b KQ - 3 11",
      "line": [],
      "spoken": "And I do think it's objectively sound.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 15,
      "t": 834.5,
      "fen": "r1bqk2r/p1pp1ppp/2p2n2/2b5/4P3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 3 8",
      "line": [],
      "spoken": "What about meeting h6 with e5? That just loses the pawn — take, take, take.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 19,
      "t": 842.5,
      "fen": "r1bq1rk1/p1pp1pp1/2p2n1p/2b3B1/4P3/2N5/PPP1BPPP/R2QK2R b KQ - 3 10",
      "line": [
        "h6",
        "Bg5",
        "O-O",
        "Be2"
      ],
      "spoken": "We simply win a pawn; at the end of the day this pawn push is never dangerous.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 23,
      "t": 845.5,
      "fen": "r1bqr1k1/p1p2pp1/2pp1n1p/2b5/4P2B/2N5/PPP1BPPP/R2Q1RK1 b - - 1 12",
      "line": [
        "Re8",
        "Bh4",
        "d6",
        "O-O"
      ],
      "spoken": "So how should White have played? White has a very hard time keeping that pawn.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 24,
      "t": 872,
      "fen": "r1bq1rk1/p1p2pp1/2pp1n1p/2b5/4P2B/2N5/PPP1BPPP/R2Q1RK1 w - - 2 13",
      "line": [
        "Rf8"
      ],
      "spoken": "A move like king h1 might be best — after g5 the bishop to g3 and g4, the idea is to win the pawn back with the bishop to f3, though the rook to d4 then hits the queen; it all looks nasty.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 23,
      "t": 873,
      "fen": "r1bqr1k1/p1p2pp1/2pp1n1p/2b5/4P2B/2N5/PPP1BPPP/R2Q1RK1 b - - 1 12",
      "line": [],
      "spoken": "The bishop to d3 apologises for the earlier bishop to e2, and transposes into a line with games in the database.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 25,
      "t": 880.5,
      "fen": "r1bqr1k1/p1p2pp1/2pp1n1p/8/1b2P2B/2NB4/PPP2PPP/R2Q1RK1 b - - 3 13",
      "line": [
        "Bb4",
        "Bd3"
      ],
      "spoken": "The bishop to b4 with f4 — I think this might even be a Sevian–Caruana game from the US Championship — so the bishop to d3 was best.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 27,
      "t": 886.5,
      "fen": "r1bqr1k1/p1p2pp1/2pp1n1p/2b5/4P2B/2N5/PPP1BPPP/R2Q1RK1 b - - 5 14",
      "line": [
        "Bc5",
        "Be2"
      ],
      "spoken": "With the bishop to c5 and White's bishop to e2...",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 29,
      "t": 888.5,
      "fen": "r1bqr1k1/p1p2p2/2pp1n1p/2b3p1/4P2B/2N2B2/PPP2PPP/R2Q1RK1 b - - 1 15",
      "line": [
        "g5",
        "Bf3"
      ],
      "spoken": "...and g5...",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 31,
      "t": 890.5,
      "fen": "r1bqr1k1/p1p2p2/2pp1n1p/2b5/4P1p1/2N2BB1/PPP2PPP/R2Q1RK1 b - - 1 16",
      "line": [
        "g4",
        "Bg3"
      ],
      "spoken": "...and g4, back to pushing all the pawns in front of my king.",
      "reanchor": true
    },
    {
      "ply": 25,
      "t": 894,
      "fen": "r1bqr1k1/p1p2pp1/2pp1n1p/8/1b2P2B/2NB4/PPP2PPP/R2Q1RK1 b - - 3 13",
      "line": [],
      "spoken": "So e5 makes our job easy — after the bishop to e2 we play the knight takes d4. We've pushed pawns in front of our king, but how is White actually going to attack? The white bishop belongs on d3, and not putting it there is White's main mistake.",
      "reanchor": true
    }
  ]
}